hi everyone welcome to biology professor  today i'm going to show you guys how to  use a q-tip  to  hand pollinate some tomato plants so you  can see i've got two tomato plants  there's one there's another  it's november right now we're inside  these plants would die outside i don't  have bees or other pollinators in my  house so i have to use these let me show  you how i do it so usually i would use  two hands i would use one hand to kind  of stabilize each flower because they  are a little fragile and the other hand  to do just what you see here i'm just  going back and forth from flower to  flower even moving from one tomato plant  over to another tomato plant  transferring pollen from the center of  one flower to the center of another  flower i'm using the same end of the  same q-tip repeatedly you might do this  every two or three days to ensure  pollination but ultimately the goal is  just to go back and forth and to  introduce pollen from one flower to  another and you should even see a little  bit of yellow on the end
 

